<h2>Building a price model</h2>
<p>A useful price model has four lines: material cost, conversion cost, certification and freight. Material cost tracks the metal or compound; conversion cost tracks energy, labour and yield; certification is a fixed cost per model; freight scales with weight and route. When a quote moves, ask which line moved. If the supplier cannot say, the quote is not a model.</p>
<h2>What to verify</h2>
<p>Check the validity date, the Incoterm, the volume tier and the documentation included. A price that excludes the COA, MSDS or UN38.3 is not comparable with one that includes them; the missing documents will appear as a cost later.</p>
